  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37144852",
      "title": "Module Summary",
      "lectureOrder": 197,
      "videoOrder": 182,
      "sourceHash": "b64589224879090649fd0b93d3b3c76799ac2c1afbba5a938682d2e4c237646a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 5.28,
          "en": "And that's it for this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.28,
          "end": 6.42,
          "en": "In this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.42,
          "end": 8.25,
          "en": "you learned about providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.25,
          "end": 10.38,
          "en": "with help of the Riverpod package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.38,
          "end": 12.93,
          "en": "which is just one of the many options you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.93,
          "end": 17.1,
          "en": "for managing global state or cross-widget state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.1,
          "end": 19.95,
          "en": "state that affects multiple widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.95,
          "end": 20.79,
          "en": "And as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.79,
          "end": 22.8,
          "en": "packages like this can be very useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.8,
          "end": 24.42,
          "en": "because in more complex apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.42,
          "end": 27.51,
          "en": "it's quite common that state changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.51,
          "end": 30.72,
          "en": "and state usage don't happen in the same widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.72,
          "end": 34.44,
          "en": "but instead might be far apart from each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.44,
          "end": 38.55,
          "en": "And in such cases, without such solutions like Riverpod,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.55,
          "end": 41.37,
          "en": "you would have to pass functions around in your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.37,
          "end": 44.43,
          "en": "so that they can be triggered from different areas",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.43,
          "end": 47.28,
          "en": "in the app than the state is needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.28,
          "end": 49.41,
          "en": "With Riverpod, you can instead set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.41,
          "end": 52.11,
          "en": "a global state management provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.11,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "so to say, which provides a dynamic value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 59.13,
          "en": "and may also provide methods for changing that value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.13,
          "end": 62.82,
          "en": "which then can be consumed from anywhere in your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.82,
          "end": 64.23,
          "en": "so that you can read",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.23,
          "end": 67.5,
          "en": "and change these values from exactly the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 70.47,
          "en": "where you need to read and change them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.47,
          "end": 72,
          "en": "For that, you learned that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72,
          "end": 74.64,
          "en": "after installing Flutter Riverpod,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.64,
          "end": 77.13,
          "en": "you must set it up here in the main.dart file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.13,
          "end": 78.75,
          "en": "by wrapping your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.75,
          "end": 82.65,
          "en": "or whichever widgets need access to this provider feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.65,
          "end": 84.363,
          "en": "with provider scope.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.41,
          "end": 88.28999999999999,
          "en": "And then you can start setting up some providers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.28999999999999,
          "end": 91.53,
          "en": "simple providers like this one here, the meals provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.53,
          "end": 95.22,
          "en": "which only returns some pretty static data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.22,
          "end": 97.2,
          "en": "or more complex providers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.2,
          "end": 100.05,
          "en": "which also allow you to change data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.05,
          "end": 101.16,
          "en": "The latter can be done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 101.16,
          "end": 105.36,
          "en": "by creating these notifier classes based on state notifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 108.363,
          "en": "combined with the state notifier provider class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.25999999999999,
          "end": 111.27000000000001,
          "en": "Either way, you have these providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 114.36,
          "en": "which then can be consumed in your widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.36,
          "end": 116.28,
          "en": "with help of the rev keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.28,
          "end": 119.67,
          "en": "which is available if you extend consumer stateful widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 119.67,
          "end": 122.88,
          "en": "and consumer state in case of stateful widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 127.05,
          "en": "or simply consumer widget in case of stateless widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.05,
          "end": 127.883,
          "en": "In that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.883,
          "end": 130.56,
          "en": "you would not have a globally available rev keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.56,
          "end": 132.27,
          "en": "but instead this second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 132.27,
          "end": 134.22,
          "en": "which you must accept in the build method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.22,
          "end": 136.35,
          "en": "which gives you this rev object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.35,
          "end": 138.93,
          "en": "and it's then this rev object which can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 138.93,
          "end": 141.12,
          "en": "to set up listeners that make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.12,
          "end": 143.13,
          "en": "that the build method is re-executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 143.13,
          "end": 145.35,
          "en": "whenever the provider data changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 145.35,
          "end": 148.323,
          "en": "and which then give you access to the provided data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 149.28,
          "end": 150.87,
          "en": "Or, as you also saw,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 150.87,
          "end": 154.47,
          "en": "you can also read values one time to then, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "also trigger those methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 158.7,
          "en": "that may change the state by reaching out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 158.7,
          "end": 161.04,
          "en": "to the notifier class that is related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 161.04,
          "end": 162.993,
          "en": "to such a notifier provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 163.98,
          "end": 167.07,
          "en": "That's how you can work with those providers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 167.07,
          "end": 169.32,
          "en": "As you learned, you can also set up providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 169.32,
          "end": 173.28,
          "en": "that depend on other providers by using this rev object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 173.28,
          "end": 176.19,
          "en": "that's automatically passed to these functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 176.19,
          "end": 179.1,
          "en": "that you must accept when setting up a provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 179.1,
          "end": 181.47,
          "en": "And with that, you now have a powerful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 181.47,
          "end": 183.96,
          "en": "cross-widget state management tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 183.96,
          "end": 186.69,
          "en": "which makes sure that you don't have to pass data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 186.69,
          "end": 189.363,
          "en": "and functions through all your widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
